    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "The Minneapolis Warehouse Historic District, roughly bounded by 1st Avenue N and 6th St N, reflects the city’s early commercial and industrial development.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.minneapolismn.gov/resident-services/property-housing/preservation/landmarks-districts/historic-districts/warehouse/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The railroad, completed in 1867, opened up opportunities that spurred the growth of the North Loop’s warehouses and factories.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.minneapolismn.gov/resident-services/property-housing/preservation/landmarks-districts/historic-districts/warehouse/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "At its peak, the Wyman Building at 400 First Avenue N housed more than twenty contemporary art galleries.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Loop%2C_Minneapolis",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Many old factories and warehouses have been converted into loft condominiums, restaurants, and shops, giving the district a mix of historic charm and modern living.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Loop%2C_Minneapolis",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The district’s architecture showcases Chicago Commercial style alongside Italianate, Queen Anne, and Richardsonian Romanesque buildings.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Loop%2C_Minneapolis",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Since the mid‑1990s, gentrification has attracted thousands of residents, turning the North Loop into a vibrant neighborhood near downtown Minneapolis.",
